# The .esc packages under internal/interop/data/std/ and
# internal/interop/data/web/ are build outputs. A converter run writes
# each one from scratch, so a one-line converter change replaces all of
# them and the resulting diff buries the change under review. Marking
# them generated collapses them by default in a pull request diff and
# drops them from the repository's language statistics.
#
# The patterns cover the two directories because the partition table in
# internal/dts_to_esc/partition.go routes a generated package to every
# .esc file under them. A hand-authored package needs a carve-out here,
# and internal/dts_to_esc/gitattributes_test.go fails until it has one.
#
# The tree is committed on purpose, so it is neither marked
# linguist-vendored nor listed in .gitignore.
internal/interop/data/std/*.esc linguist-generated=true
internal/interop/data/web/*.esc linguist-generated=true
